/E (50. Why is clock domain crossing \(CDC\) verification crucial in automotive chips?)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
716 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1166 0 R
/E (CDC errors in automotive SoCs \(e.g., ADAS processors\) can cause random failures due to metastability.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
717 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1167 0 R
/E (Example: A self-driving car's camera module communicates at 200 MHz, while its AI processor runs at 1 GHz. Improper CDC handling could cause image processing glitches, leading to incorrect object detection.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
